Notebook[{
Cell["ArrayDomain", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"24ce4eff-0006-df4e-ab5f-43c361b2bd83"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayDomain", "[", "arr", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"181e9321-2e01-c649-a02d-e0f677107977"],
 " ",
 "gives the narrowest recognized value domain containing every entry of arr, \
or \"Expression\" if the entries lie in none of them."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"fd7530d1-359e-4347-a945-79487726cd66"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"0eb63707-67b2-8448-8c57-61b68591a841"],

Cell["\<\
The recognized domains are \"Boolean\", \"Integer\", \"Rational\", \"Real\" \
and \"Complex\", together with FiniteField[p, n].\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f25df53b-a3e2-7c41-9233-763f647ee02c"],

Cell["\<\
\"Boolean\" means the entries are True and False. Entries 0 and 1 are \
integers, and the elements of the two-element field are FiniteField[2, 1].\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0f2b6f61-17c7-ba41-bd9b-5c2b692f376c"],

Cell["\<\
It is computed from the entries, not declared: an array is not told what it \
is made of. An array whose entries answer to none of the recognized domains \
is an array of expressions, which is a perfectly good array; generated \
symbolic entries and labels are both of that kind.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7609b3d7-fa4c-de4e-a3a3-5330a52c7406"],

Cell["\<\
Because it is computed rather than stored, it costs a pass over the entries \
to ask.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7ca9d574-4dea-5d45-8c7b-c2cca8ec650f"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"194762bb-8e5b-d04a-b183-e0d346f9e9f2"],

Cell["\<\
ArrayDomain @ ArrayObject[#] & /@ {{True, False}, {1, 2}, {1/2, 3}, {1.5, 2}, \
{1 + I, 2}}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"fbba7d96-f5a4-e742-9954-b1a0a9979db3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"Boolean\"\>", ",", "\<\"Integer\"\>", ",", "\<\"Rational\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"Real\"\>", ",", "\<\"Complex\"\>"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionU\
UID->"2a355905-88d1-be4e-bba2-d87c25195451"],

Cell["Entries of a finite field:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"9bf27e69-e1df-1f45-b452-5fd4b571e693"],

Cell["\<\
ArrayDomain @ ArrayObject[{FiniteField[2, 1][0], FiniteField[2, 1][1]}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"48d37e3f-7547-1340-95d7-b8e210cbb88d"],

